WEBVTT

00:00:02.040 --> 00:00:05.520
April 20, 1648 Testament Era
4:58 A.M., Sagarmatha Corridor

00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:08.820
5:00 A.M.
Asama Shrine, Okutama

00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:14.510
Same Time
Tomo Asama's Room

00:00:19.430 --> 00:00:22.390
That morning was the same as any other.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:26.940
Toorimase, toorimase

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:26.940
Let us pass, let us pass

00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:25.790
Nothing particularly stood out.

00:00:26.420 --> 00:00:28.280
Everything looked like usual.

00:00:26.940 --> 00:00:33.280
Ikaba izuko ga hosomichi nareba

00:00:26.940 --> 00:00:33.280
Where doth this narrow path lead?

00:00:31.710 --> 00:00:35.160
I thought days such as this would last forever,

00:00:33.580 --> 00:00:40.260
Tenjin moto he to itaru hosomichi

00:00:33.580 --> 00:00:40.260
It doth lead to the gods in Heaven

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:36.510
but they shatter as

00:00:38.350 --> 00:00:39.790
they draw to an end.

00:00:40.570 --> 00:00:46.780
Goiken gomuyou toorenu totemo

00:00:40.570 --> 00:00:46.780
Thou thoughts matter not for ye cannot pass

00:00:42.880 --> 00:00:45.710
When the time comes, I...

00:01:07.250 --> 00:01:10.250
Nani ga mieru?

00:01:07.250 --> 00:01:10.250
What do you see?

00:01:10.250 --> 00:01:13.480
Ari no mama no kimi wa

00:01:10.250 --> 00:01:13.480
You've closed yourself off to love

00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:19.560
Tsuyoku naru made itoshisa wo tojite

00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:19.560
Until you grow innately strong

00:01:19.560 --> 00:01:22.650
Nani wo kiku no?

00:01:19.560 --> 00:01:22.650
What are you listening to?

00:01:22.650 --> 00:01:25.730
Himitsu no kobeya de

00:01:22.650 --> 00:01:25.730
Shall I tell you about days long past

00:01:25.730 --> 00:01:31.490
Inishie no hibi katarou ka?

00:01:25.730 --> 00:01:31.490
In our secret little room?

00:01:31.780 --> 00:01:34.780
Kioku ni dakarete

00:01:31.780 --> 00:01:34.780
Embraced in memories

00:01:34.780 --> 00:01:38.080
Kudakareta mysteria

00:01:34.780 --> 00:01:38.080
The mysteria crumbles

00:01:38.080 --> 00:01:40.770
Higeki wo koete

00:01:38.080 --> 00:01:40.770
Once you overcome this tragedy

00:01:40.770 --> 00:01:43.040
Odayaka na inori

00:01:40.770 --> 00:01:43.040
Offer a gentle prayer

00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:47.000
Owari ga hajimari

00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:47.000
Endings are just beginnings

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:50.510
Shinsekai de hito wa mirai wo

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:50.510
People toss aside all they have

00:01:50.510 --> 00:01:52.840
Bishu no you ni

00:01:50.510 --> 00:01:52.840
Without ever knowing

00:01:52.840 --> 00:01:56.470
Nomi hoseru ka sae shirazu

00:01:52.840 --> 00:01:56.470
If they could drink up the new world

00:01:56.470 --> 00:01:59.470
Subete houri nageta

00:01:56.470 --> 00:01:59.470
Like a savory wine

00:01:59.470 --> 00:02:02.630
Shinsekai wa tsumetai risei to

00:01:59.470 --> 00:02:02.630
The new world resides

00:02:02.630 --> 00:02:05.350
Kiseki no hazama

00:02:02.630 --> 00:02:05.350
Between boring logic and miracles

00:02:05.570 --> 00:02:14.360
Doushite koko de kimi to aeta no

00:02:05.570 --> 00:02:14.360
I wonder why this is where I first met you

00:02:18.680 --> 00:02:22.180
2:12 P.M.
Musashi Ariadust Academy

00:02:26.930 --> 00:02:31.230
Commandos in Town

00:02:34.230 --> 00:02:36.990
2:15 P.M.
Musashi Ariadust Academy Student Dorms

00:02:34.990 --> 00:02:36.340
Found it.

00:02:43.510 --> 00:02:44.600
Yes?

00:02:44.970 --> 00:02:46.440
I'm sorry!

00:02:46.440 --> 00:02:48.520
I must have the wrong room.

00:02:48.520 --> 00:02:49.770
Sorry!

00:02:51.950 --> 00:02:54.070
That's Miriam?

00:02:54.170 --> 00:02:55.460
Musashi Ariadust Academy Student Dorm:
Okutama 1-15-26

00:02:55.790 --> 00:02:59.280
I wonder who I should bring this up with?

00:03:01.590 --> 00:03:04.720
2:17 P.M.
Highway to Kakamigahara Checkpoint No.1, Mikawa

00:03:01.760 --> 00:03:04.740
Wow, I'm surprised that Yasumasa Sakakibara

00:03:05.110 --> 00:03:06.570
and Tadakatsu Honda of the

00:03:06.570 --> 00:03:09.370
Four Divine Matsudaira Kings would come see me.

00:03:09.880 --> 00:03:11.540
Where's Ii?

00:03:11.800 --> 00:03:14.110
Well you see, Mr. Sakai...

00:03:14.110 --> 00:03:16.420
You needn't explain, Sakakibara.

00:03:17.750 --> 00:03:18.670
Show me!

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:21.140
Whoa, whoa, whoa, Dacchan!

00:03:21.140 --> 00:03:23.930
Nothing ever ends well when you say that.

00:03:39.030 --> 00:03:39.990
Score!

00:03:45.020 --> 00:03:47.470
Phew, that was close!

00:03:47.470 --> 00:03:50.620
So, what's the meaning of this?

00:03:51.690 --> 00:03:55.130
2:37 P.M.
Residential District, Tama

00:03:51.910 --> 00:03:55.130
Seriously though,
don't you think this is a bit much?

00:03:55.480 --> 00:03:57.440
This should be about right.

00:03:57.440 --> 00:03:59.050
After all, we're having a party tomorrow.

00:03:59.180 --> 00:04:00.520
A party, eh?

00:04:00.520 --> 00:04:03.250
I hope it will be a fun one.

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:08.660
The sky sure is busy.

00:04:08.940 --> 00:04:11.830
Tres España's Gods of War left their posts,

00:04:11.830 --> 00:04:15.310
so the deliverers are
holding races and mock battles.

00:04:16.450 --> 00:04:18.070
Naruse and Naito might be up there.

00:04:18.470 --> 00:04:22.100
I bet they'll show up at the Academy later tonight too.

00:04:22.100 --> 00:04:22.610
Yeah!

00:04:23.320 --> 00:04:25.320
Mikawa's shooting fireworks,

00:04:25.320 --> 00:04:28.240
but it looks like everyone's hanging out
with the Chancellor instead.

00:04:28.240 --> 00:04:29.790
I..I'm going too!

00:04:30.060 --> 00:04:33.500
Everyone is truly worried for Tori.

00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:38.470
The world's bustling over Oda,
the Armor of Deadly Sins and Armageddon.

00:04:38.470 --> 00:04:43.470
And here we are,
worried if a certain moron will get the girl.

00:04:43.770 --> 00:04:46.260
It may not be a Song of Passage, but it's still scary.

00:04:48.470 --> 00:04:52.900
I wonder how Tori feels about this confession?

00:04:53.560 --> 00:04:58.310
Is it a new beginning or a change of heart?

00:04:58.880 --> 00:05:01.680
I bet Kimi is ready to accept whatever happens.

00:05:01.680 --> 00:05:06.780
She's the one who'll be put out the most
if it all goes well for Tori tomorrow.

00:05:07.060 --> 00:05:10.540
But even so, that idiot isn't out here with us.

00:05:11.460 --> 00:05:14.200
She's still sitting on the stairs, isn't she?

00:05:15.030 --> 00:05:19.880
Yeah, when we adjourned Tori said
he was gonna check out Remorse Way.

00:05:20.130 --> 00:05:24.450
That moron hasn't gone there
since the accident ten years ago.

00:05:24.450 --> 00:05:26.430
But Kimi is...

00:05:26.430 --> 00:05:31.480
She's watching as his stupid sister
to see if her moronic brother

00:05:31.480 --> 00:05:33.300
can do it or not.

00:05:34.460 --> 00:05:38.560
I think everything goes back to Horizon.

00:05:39.450 --> 00:05:44.360
Horizon was a kind person.

00:05:45.480 --> 00:05:47.280
D..Did you know?

00:05:47.630 --> 00:05:50.460
Whenever Tori starts talking to me,

00:05:50.460 --> 00:05:55.750
he always says, "Hey!" or "So like" without fail.

00:05:56.330 --> 00:06:00.420
And when he offers me his hand or gets ready to go,

00:06:00.420 --> 00:06:02.020
he does this.

00:06:03.690 --> 00:06:06.600
That's his sign.

00:06:07.400 --> 00:06:10.310
I can't see,

00:06:10.310 --> 00:06:13.430
so he does that to give me a heads up.

00:06:13.780 --> 00:06:17.550
Yeah, and we started following suit.

00:06:17.900 --> 00:06:21.260
Horizon was the one who started that.

00:06:27.710 --> 00:06:32.910
Even though Horizon's gone,
Tori hasn't forgotten about her.

00:06:33.990 --> 00:06:35.190
Indeed.

00:06:36.280 --> 00:06:37.790
Huh?

00:06:38.230 --> 00:06:40.170
You were out shopping too?

00:06:40.440 --> 00:06:44.420
Just how big are you gonna make tomorrow's party?

00:06:44.420 --> 00:06:46.380
We're going to be buried in food!

00:06:47.140 --> 00:06:48.880
What's going on?

00:06:48.880 --> 00:06:51.430
I've had a lot of customers from the
Academy since this morning!

00:06:51.730 --> 00:06:53.220
Sorry!

00:06:53.220 --> 00:06:57.020
Actually, we might be causing quite
the ruckus here tomorrow.

00:06:57.410 --> 00:06:59.470
Are you holding a party or something?

00:06:59.470 --> 00:07:03.600
Then, I might have to ask P-01s to go all-out.

00:07:04.650 --> 00:07:05.740
A party?

00:07:06.050 --> 00:07:07.490
I guess.

00:07:07.810 --> 00:07:10.400
Yes, I believe everything will work out!

00:07:11.070 --> 00:07:15.020
After all, everyone is hoping that it will be fun party.

00:07:15.680 --> 00:07:18.230
Niello Trade

00:07:15.680 --> 00:07:18.230
2:27 P.M.
Transportation District, Murayama

00:07:18.230 --> 00:07:19.110
I know!

00:07:18.230 --> 00:07:21.170
Niello Trade

00:07:19.110 --> 00:07:21.170
I think this is gonna be a blast!

00:07:21.610 --> 00:07:24.380
So, Gacchan, aren't they holding a

00:07:24.380 --> 00:07:27.120
rising altitude race in the weighted atmosphere?

00:07:27.120 --> 00:07:28.380
Wanna enter?

00:07:28.630 --> 00:07:29.760
<i>Sounds good.</i>

00:07:29.760 --> 00:07:31.940
<i>Let's enter another one after work.</i>

00:07:31.940 --> 00:07:34.440
<i>We can make some money off
the Admirals and Marines.</i>

00:07:34.440 --> 00:07:35.470
Here, Thanks.

00:07:35.790 --> 00:07:36.560
Later!

00:07:38.200 --> 00:07:41.090
Say, Gacchan, can you see Kimi?

00:07:41.800 --> 00:07:42.600
Judge.

00:07:42.940 --> 00:07:45.610
I can see her clearly since she hasn't moved.

00:07:45.970 --> 00:07:49.120
Doesn't that mean the Chancellor hasn't budged?

00:07:49.120 --> 00:07:51.810
Sure does. Care to make a comment?

00:07:51.810 --> 00:07:52.870
You bet I do!

00:07:52.870 --> 00:07:55.840
I've got a rush delivery for the Student Council.

00:07:54.910 --> 00:07:56.870
Working Class Man

00:07:55.840 --> 00:07:57.320
The shipping label clearly says,

00:07:57.320 --> 00:08:01.810
"Highest Peak! The Virgin Queen
Elizabeth, 1st Edition."

00:08:02.160 --> 00:08:04.230
I bet the Chancellor ordered this.

00:08:04.440 --> 00:08:07.540
Please decide if you're going to
feel bad for him or poke fun at him.

00:08:07.800 --> 00:08:11.120
It was camouflaged in an
educational program's package,

00:08:11.120 --> 00:08:13.230
but he botched up the label.

00:08:13.230 --> 00:08:14.260
So it seems...

00:08:14.400 --> 00:08:16.220
Oh, it's Seijun!

00:08:17.790 --> 00:08:18.680
Hey!

00:08:19.370 --> 00:08:20.580
What's up?

00:08:21.610 --> 00:08:23.100
I just got back from Mikawa.

00:08:23.270 --> 00:08:25.800
Margot, is Masazumi there?

00:08:25.800 --> 00:08:27.560
Tell her about tonight and that package.

00:08:27.840 --> 00:08:31.970
Seijun, the Chancellor's exorcising
ghosts at school tonight.

00:08:31.970 --> 00:08:32.930
You coming?

00:08:32.930 --> 00:08:36.040
Uh, no, I live in Murayama,

00:08:36.040 --> 00:08:38.140
so I'd have to go through the guard post

00:08:38.140 --> 00:08:39.930
in order to visit Okutama at night.

00:08:39.930 --> 00:08:42.450
That would put my father out.

00:08:42.660 --> 00:08:46.190
Isn't your dad a big shot on the Provisional Council?

00:08:46.190 --> 00:08:47.800
Uh, I guess...

00:08:48.110 --> 00:08:49.620
Then, this is for you.

00:08:49.620 --> 00:08:51.170
It's addressed to the Student Council.

00:08:51.190 --> 00:08:53.880
To: Student Council
Breakable! "Highest Peak!
The Virgin Queen Elizabeth,
1st Edition."
Lightning Delivery

00:08:51.710 --> 00:08:53.880
Why is this going to the Student Council?!

00:08:54.110 --> 00:08:58.080
The Chancellor oughta be
near Remorse Way about now.

00:08:58.080 --> 00:08:59.950
I think you should go see him.

00:08:59.950 --> 00:09:00.640
Why?

00:09:01.020 --> 00:09:02.560
Because, Seijun...

00:09:06.300 --> 00:09:08.270
Whoa! What's going on?!

00:09:08.740 --> 00:09:09.730
A race!

00:09:11.440 --> 00:09:13.690
C'mon, little missy!

00:09:14.550 --> 00:09:17.000
Pass that on to the Chancellor!

00:09:16.930 --> 00:09:17.590
Ritual Summons
Work's Title
"When One Falls Asleep"
Operate 5 Times

00:09:38.410 --> 00:09:40.880
The Chancellor and Kimi, eh?

00:09:46.750 --> 00:09:49.360
3:03 P.M.
Musashi Ariadust Academy Student Dorms

00:09:51.740 --> 00:09:53.240
You should come in.

00:09:53.240 --> 00:09:54.110
What's keeping you?

00:09:55.390 --> 00:09:57.140
A..Are you sure?

00:10:03.910 --> 00:10:08.210
Um, the Academy said I'm supposed
to stay here as of today.

00:10:08.390 --> 00:10:09.510
That's fine.

00:10:09.510 --> 00:10:12.040
It's not like I've never shared a room before.

00:10:12.350 --> 00:10:14.780
Although, it will be my first time with a boy.

00:10:14.780 --> 00:10:15.880
In..In that case...

00:10:16.480 --> 00:10:18.010
We'll simply have to adjust.

00:10:18.320 --> 00:10:21.300
A..Are you sure you don't mind living with a boy?

00:10:21.610 --> 00:10:23.590
Would you leave if I asked?

00:10:23.590 --> 00:10:27.620
After you first arrived,
you went and requested a different room.

00:10:27.620 --> 00:10:31.760
But it was rejected,
so you've been standing out by the door.

00:10:31.760 --> 00:10:32.700
Y..Yeah...

00:10:33.370 --> 00:10:38.210
I'd like you to promise me something, okay?

00:10:38.600 --> 00:10:39.490
Promise?

00:10:39.780 --> 00:10:40.770
Right.

00:10:40.770 --> 00:10:43.540
We mustn't interfere with each
other's personal affairs.

00:10:43.540 --> 00:10:44.650
Let's see...

00:10:44.650 --> 00:10:46.300
An extreme example would be

00:10:46.300 --> 00:10:50.920
that I can't complain even if you bring in a girl.

00:10:50.920 --> 00:10:53.190
I'd never do that!

00:10:54.380 --> 00:10:55.500
I'm teasing!

00:10:56.910 --> 00:10:58.840
Do you know what I admire?

00:11:00.960 --> 00:11:02.760
Dense, earnest people.

00:11:04.690 --> 00:11:05.760
Uh...

00:11:06.120 --> 00:11:10.480
Yes, I don't question those who are dense and earnest.

00:11:21.630 --> 00:11:24.400
You may come back if you're afraid,

00:11:24.400 --> 00:11:25.780
my foolish brother.

00:11:26.960 --> 00:11:27.840
Whoo!

00:11:29.740 --> 00:11:30.790
Huh?

00:11:33.200 --> 00:11:36.820
You just had to destroy the mood
right when it was getting good.

00:11:36.820 --> 00:11:38.420
What's Tori doing?

00:11:38.850 --> 00:11:40.630
Is that some new game?

00:11:40.630 --> 00:11:42.680
Or should I go whack 'im?

00:11:44.010 --> 00:11:47.270
Ma'am, I heard you were drinking in the cafeteria,

00:11:47.270 --> 00:11:49.030
so what brought you out here?

00:11:49.430 --> 00:11:52.770
To cool down, I guess.

00:11:55.140 --> 00:11:57.690
Ma'am, you shouldn't use your hands!

00:11:58.080 --> 00:11:59.760
It will damage your hair.

00:11:59.760 --> 00:12:01.450
Just leave it to me.

00:12:08.350 --> 00:12:10.880
What is it, Ma'am? That's creepy.

00:12:11.180 --> 00:12:12.390
Well see,

00:12:12.390 --> 00:12:15.090
I was just remembering how an old lady

00:12:15.090 --> 00:12:17.170
in my neighborhood used to do this.

00:12:18.590 --> 00:12:21.380
Ma'am, being drunk is no excuse

00:12:21.380 --> 00:12:23.660
for comparing me with an old woman.

00:12:27.610 --> 00:12:29.010
What is it?

00:12:29.600 --> 00:12:32.020
You can do it. You can...

00:12:33.390 --> 00:12:36.050
Ma'am, are you my foolish brother's ally?

00:12:36.050 --> 00:12:38.020
You bet I am!

00:12:38.020 --> 00:12:43.430
I'll always side with everyone in your class,
not just Tori.

00:12:43.430 --> 00:12:47.720
Oh, but I can't directly interfere
with any student contention.

00:12:47.720 --> 00:12:48.530
What's this?

00:12:51.640 --> 00:12:53.250
It's Masazumi.

00:12:56.190 --> 00:12:59.440
3:35 P.M.
Spiritual Shrine Heian, Okutama

00:13:00.170 --> 00:13:02.170
Spiritual Shrine
1618 Hei—

00:13:04.260 --> 00:13:05.760
Shomen Street

00:13:05.930 --> 00:13:08.030
I'm on the right path.

00:13:13.180 --> 00:13:20.460
Kono ko no too no oiwai ni

00:13:13.180 --> 00:13:20.460
To celebrate this child's tenth

00:13:19.050 --> 00:13:20.490
P-01s?

00:13:20.460 --> 00:13:27.240
I must make an offering with these talismans

00:13:20.460 --> 00:13:27.240
Ryou no ofuda wo osame ni sanzu

00:13:27.240 --> 00:13:33.740
The path out is pleasant, but returning is scary

00:13:27.240 --> 00:13:33.740
Iki wa yoi nagi, kaeri wa kowaki

00:13:33.740 --> 00:13:43.870
Can I pass despite my fears?

00:13:33.740 --> 00:13:43.870
Waga naka kowaki no tooshi kana?

00:13:36.840 --> 00:13:38.090
Out at last!

00:13:41.250 --> 00:13:44.630
I feel like I've heard her voice a lot today.

00:13:51.760 --> 00:13:54.850
What are you doing here, Masazumi?

00:13:56.280 --> 00:13:57.140
Father!

00:13:57.840 --> 00:14:00.820
There is still much for me to learn about Musashi,

00:14:00.820 --> 00:14:02.610
so I was investigating the area.

00:14:03.110 --> 00:14:06.280
Did you learn anything about the rest area in those woods

00:14:06.280 --> 00:14:07.950
you just stumbled out of?

00:14:08.610 --> 00:14:10.580
What about that rest area?

00:14:11.420 --> 00:14:13.340
Your studies were insufficient

00:14:13.340 --> 00:14:15.290
if you didn't learn anything.

00:14:15.900 --> 00:14:16.830
Sir...

00:14:17.920 --> 00:14:22.350
Your son is holding a most unusual item.

00:14:22.350 --> 00:14:23.130
Huh?

00:14:23.260 --> 00:14:27.470
I accept items like that in my business deals.

00:14:27.470 --> 00:14:29.930
To: Student Council
Breakable! "Highest Peak!
The Virgin Queen Elizabeth,
1st Edition."
Lightning Delivery

00:14:27.820 --> 00:14:29.930
The first edition is most rare!

00:14:30.310 --> 00:14:31.590
Oh, no, this is...

00:14:31.590 --> 00:14:34.060
I'm unfamiliar with it, but give it to him.

00:14:36.920 --> 00:14:39.470
But this is my friend's...

00:14:39.930 --> 00:14:40.960
Masazumi!

00:14:52.680 --> 00:14:53.450
Hey!

00:14:54.330 --> 00:14:55.330
Huh?

00:14:55.680 --> 00:14:58.160
Sweet! Good job, Seijun!

00:14:58.240 --> 00:14:59.240
Thanks a bunch!

00:14:59.240 --> 00:15:00.440
I just gotta play this tonight,

00:15:00.440 --> 00:15:02.880
but Naito and Naruse were taking forever!

00:15:03.190 --> 00:15:05.560
Aoi, you look awful!

00:15:05.560 --> 00:15:06.420
Are you okay?

00:15:06.420 --> 00:15:08.670
Don't worry, I'm winded from running!

00:15:09.190 --> 00:15:12.010
Tomorrow, I'm gonna tell the girl I love how I feel.

00:15:12.010 --> 00:15:14.100
So, we're partying on campus tonight.

00:15:14.100 --> 00:15:14.970
You coming?

00:15:14.970 --> 00:15:16.570
Of course not!

00:15:16.570 --> 00:15:17.950
It's against school rules.

00:15:17.950 --> 00:15:19.990
If I'm going anywhere, it's to see Mikawa's fireworks.

00:15:21.320 --> 00:15:23.400
I was really hoping you'd make it.

00:15:23.660 --> 00:15:26.320
You know the girl I'm gonna confess to uber well.

00:15:26.900 --> 00:15:28.820
W..Wait a sec!

00:15:28.820 --> 00:15:30.810
This won't put me out any, will it?

00:15:30.810 --> 00:15:33.660
I can't say!

00:15:37.860 --> 00:15:39.230
I'm sorry about that.

00:15:39.230 --> 00:15:40.390
No worries.

00:15:40.390 --> 00:15:43.970
I'm surprised to see the
Master of Remorse Way out here.

00:15:44.260 --> 00:15:46.110
It's been a good decade!

00:15:46.340 --> 00:15:48.970
The Master of Remorse Way?

00:15:50.290 --> 00:15:52.280
Look there yonder.

00:15:52.580 --> 00:15:53.390
Okay...

00:15:53.940 --> 00:15:58.700
A girl died in an accident around here a long time ago.

00:15:58.700 --> 00:16:00.430
The one on the monument?

00:16:00.430 --> 00:16:01.020
Judge.

00:16:01.650 --> 00:16:05.000
Her name was Horizon Ariadust.

00:16:05.340 --> 00:16:07.270
Isn't Ariadust the Academy's name?

00:16:07.810 --> 00:16:11.780
When Lord Motonobu became the head
of Mikawa thirty years ago,

00:16:11.780 --> 00:16:14.020
he removed the first syllable in the Matsudaira name

00:16:14.020 --> 00:16:15.980
and flipped it backwards.

00:16:15.980 --> 00:16:19.720
Thus, he changed his name from
Matsudaira to Ariadust.

00:16:19.720 --> 00:16:22.960
It was to show his allegiance to the Testament Union.

00:16:23.390 --> 00:16:25.890
The Testament Union acknowledged his

00:16:25.890 --> 00:16:27.900
firm resolution and flipped his name back,

00:16:27.900 --> 00:16:31.280
but there were some who kept that name.

00:16:31.860 --> 00:16:33.590
Haven't you heard?

00:16:33.880 --> 00:16:37.050
Lord Motonobu had a common-law wife and child.

00:16:37.600 --> 00:16:38.760
Well...

00:16:39.250 --> 00:16:42.060
The child's name was Horizon Ariadust.

00:16:42.250 --> 00:16:43.330
Don't forget it!

00:16:44.900 --> 00:16:48.650
Lady Horizon got into an accident
with Lord Motonobu's carriage.

00:16:49.320 --> 00:16:53.280
He was headed for a function celebrating
Musashi's approval for repairs.

00:17:01.160 --> 00:17:03.750
It will have been ten years tomorrow.

00:17:03.980 --> 00:17:05.760
It was a long time ago,

00:17:05.760 --> 00:17:10.690
but it must replay in real time
for the Master of Remorse Way.

00:17:10.690 --> 00:17:12.250
Going by the end result,

00:17:12.250 --> 00:17:15.240
he killed Lady Horizon.

00:17:16.770 --> 00:17:19.850
What do you mean he killed her?

00:17:23.010 --> 00:17:27.350
Then what's the secret behind
everyone's words "pursue the truth"?

00:17:27.750 --> 00:17:30.490
It's about Tori Aoi's "remorse."

00:17:30.760 --> 00:17:34.190
It's a dual meaning playing on
words with Remorse Way.

00:17:37.170 --> 00:17:39.760
He was also injured when they rushed him

00:17:39.760 --> 00:17:41.450
and Lady Horizon to Mikawa.

00:17:41.840 --> 00:17:44.640
But he came back alone.

00:17:44.640 --> 00:17:46.330
All that remained was his remorse.

00:17:47.670 --> 00:17:52.180
Then, how is he able to still laugh?

00:17:53.680 --> 00:17:56.930
Why does everyone offer him their support?

00:17:57.320 --> 00:17:59.530
"Why," eh?

00:18:00.160 --> 00:18:02.310
Will you pursue this, Masazumi,

00:18:02.860 --> 00:18:04.950
and see where his remorse takes him?

00:18:05.350 --> 00:18:07.010
I'm running late for my meeting.

00:18:07.010 --> 00:18:07.810
We're finished here.

00:18:12.620 --> 00:18:17.900
So, I'm still in the dark, aren't I?

00:18:21.890 --> 00:18:25.540
6:09 P.M.
Above the Normal Land Port, Mikawa

00:18:34.930 --> 00:18:36.480
Isn't that...

00:18:36.720 --> 00:18:38.890
Indeed, it is the "Peerless Man of the East"

00:18:38.890 --> 00:18:42.040
Tadakatsu Honda's daughter, Futayo Honda.

00:18:42.590 --> 00:18:47.540
More importantly,
please stand proudly and look forward,

00:18:47.540 --> 00:18:50.510
"Peerless Man of the West" Muneshige Tachibana.

00:18:52.020 --> 00:18:53.570
I know.

00:18:53.830 --> 00:18:58.400
My current job is to keep a check on
Mikawa and the Pope President.

00:18:58.950 --> 00:19:01.050
Despite my inability to do anything but fight,

00:19:01.050 --> 00:19:04.540
they treat me like quite the political piece.

00:19:06.140 --> 00:19:07.710
Please do not lose.

00:19:08.650 --> 00:19:10.620
Do not bring me sadness.

00:19:13.640 --> 00:19:14.510
Very well.

00:19:16.490 --> 00:19:20.240
7:00 P.M.
Kakamigahara Guard Post, Mikawa

00:19:18.590 --> 00:19:20.590
<i>B1T3 to B2T3.</i>

00:19:20.830 --> 00:19:22.660
<i>We're on duty, so no standing.</i>

00:19:22.660 --> 00:19:23.940
<i>I can see you from here!</i>

00:19:25.340 --> 00:19:27.370
But I was sitting!

00:19:38.130 --> 00:19:41.090
7:30 P.M.
Musashi Ariadust Academy

00:19:38.990 --> 00:19:41.450
So then, is everyone here?

00:19:41.450 --> 00:19:42.680
Judge!

00:19:42.680 --> 00:19:44.820
Tori isn't here yet.

00:19:44.820 --> 00:19:48.180
And what'd you do with the
elementary schoolers living here?

00:19:48.180 --> 00:19:50.690
Fool! Their parents are what matter!

00:19:50.690 --> 00:19:52.000
They pay the bills.

00:19:52.000 --> 00:19:53.780
Shiro, you rock!

00:19:53.780 --> 00:19:55.340
Excuse me...

00:19:55.830 --> 00:19:56.950
What is it, Asama?

00:19:56.950 --> 00:20:01.130
I'd like to warn everyone about something
before we begin the exorcism.

00:20:01.500 --> 00:20:02.930
Fine, go ahead.

00:20:02.930 --> 00:20:04.390
But don't spend any money.

00:20:04.390 --> 00:20:05.850
No, I won't.

00:20:06.230 --> 00:20:09.960
You know how rumor has it
the end of the world is coming?

00:20:09.960 --> 00:20:12.440
Supernatural events have been
occurring across the land.

00:20:12.990 --> 00:20:15.100
One you should be aware of is a form of

00:20:15.100 --> 00:20:17.780
being spirited away called "Lost Nobles."

00:20:18.120 --> 00:20:21.840
We normally consider these events urban legends,

00:20:21.280 --> 00:20:24.950
Lost Nobles

00:20:21.840 --> 00:20:24.950
but last year a case was reported in the Far East.

00:20:25.800 --> 00:20:28.240
It was Masazumi's mother.

00:20:29.600 --> 00:20:32.210
I..I can't hear you!

00:20:31.190 --> 00:20:33.810
Kimi, I know you can't stand scary stories, but still!

00:20:33.810 --> 00:20:35.090
Pipe down over there!

00:20:35.090 --> 00:20:35.880
Be quiet!

00:20:35.880 --> 00:20:37.240
Kimi, calm down!

00:20:37.240 --> 00:20:38.960
Okay, I'm late!

00:20:38.960 --> 00:20:40.070
Sorry, my bad!

00:20:40.070 --> 00:20:41.750
The prep took a while.

00:20:41.750 --> 00:20:43.050
Let's get started!

00:20:43.440 --> 00:20:45.900
He isn't hiding that he set traps, is he?

00:20:46.360 --> 00:20:47.360
Nope...

00:20:47.780 --> 00:20:51.040
7:44 P.M.
Hallway in Front of the Library

00:20:49.540 --> 00:20:51.230
How's it look, Asamachi?

00:20:51.520 --> 00:20:54.590
I haven't seen a damn thing.

00:20:54.590 --> 00:20:58.120
I hope it's easy to identify,
like the sound of something wrapping.

00:20:58.120 --> 00:21:01.500
I..I can't handle noises!

00:21:01.500 --> 00:21:02.770
It's okay.

00:21:02.770 --> 00:21:04.960
There's nothing around here.

00:21:04.960 --> 00:21:07.980
But well, over there...

00:21:13.000 --> 00:21:13.950
Bull's eye!

00:21:13.950 --> 00:21:15.110
Wh..What?!

00:21:15.110 --> 00:21:16.580
What was over there?!

00:21:16.580 --> 00:21:18.180
You don't need to worry about it.

00:21:18.180 --> 00:21:21.400
You'll be fine as long as you stay close.

00:21:21.400 --> 00:21:23.850
That doesn't make me feel any better!

00:21:24.540 --> 00:21:29.190
Adele, you shoulda brought your mechanic shell
if you're so freaked out.

00:21:29.190 --> 00:21:33.320
Nah, it's an older model so it's insanely heavy.

00:21:33.320 --> 00:21:34.520
Whoa!

00:21:34.520 --> 00:21:36.730
Library

00:21:35.500 --> 00:21:36.730
The library?

00:21:37.330 --> 00:21:40.990
Right, this is where our job ends.

00:21:44.470 --> 00:21:45.490
Now, then...

00:21:56.150 --> 00:21:57.120
What are they?

00:21:58.950 --> 00:22:01.090
We got new values!

00:22:07.460 --> 00:22:09.970
Hey, moron! What'd you do?!

00:22:09.970 --> 00:22:11.400
I didn't do a thing.

00:22:11.400 --> 00:22:12.390
I asked them to!

00:22:12.820 --> 00:22:13.870
Who?!

00:22:13.870 --> 00:22:16.080
It better be someone we can pay off.

00:22:16.080 --> 00:22:17.550
Ya-hoo!

00:22:17.550 --> 00:22:18.480
Huh?

00:22:20.090 --> 00:22:21.860
Yah-haa!

00:22:27.320 --> 00:22:29.530
Until then, I believed

00:22:30.500 --> 00:22:34.350
we wouldn't change even
if Tori confessed his feelings.

00:22:34.830 --> 00:22:37.300
I thought the world would never change.

00:22:38.600 --> 00:22:40.900
7:59 P.M.
Shin-Nagoya Castle, Mikawa

00:22:40.830 --> 00:22:44.830
And that we would greet a happy tomorrow as always.

00:22:46.660 --> 00:22:50.820
Sora ni nozomu you ni

00:22:46.660 --> 00:22:50.820
Our voyage across the real world

00:22:51.100 --> 00:22:57.830
Koukai suru genjitsu sekai no tabi

00:22:51.100 --> 00:22:57.830
Is like navigating straight for the sky

00:22:58.330 --> 00:23:02.170
Nani mo mottenai kedo

00:22:58.330 --> 00:23:02.170
I may not have anything

00:23:02.680 --> 00:23:05.280
Kokoro no naka

00:23:02.680 --> 00:23:05.280
But I have a dream

00:23:05.280 --> 00:23:09.510
Kagayaita yume ga aru yo

00:23:05.280 --> 00:23:09.510
That's shone brightly in my heart

00:23:09.760 --> 00:23:12.350
Mada kikoenai

00:23:09.760 --> 00:23:12.350
I still haven't heard

00:23:12.350 --> 00:23:15.840
Kimi no hontou no mune no koe

00:23:12.350 --> 00:23:15.840
The voice spoken from your heart

00:23:16.140 --> 00:23:20.760
Shiritain da — sugao wo misete yo

00:23:16.140 --> 00:23:20.760
Let me in — show me the real you

00:23:20.760 --> 00:23:24.350
Barabara ni chirabatta

00:23:20.760 --> 00:23:24.350
We'll bury the void

00:23:24.350 --> 00:23:27.450
Ikutsu mo no piisu wo

00:23:24.350 --> 00:23:27.450
As we find all of the pieces

00:23:27.620 --> 00:23:30.120
Hitotsu zutsu sagashite

00:23:27.620 --> 00:23:30.120
That have gotten scattered around

00:23:30.120 --> 00:23:33.280
Kuuhaku wo umete iku no sa

00:23:30.120 --> 00:23:33.280
One piece at a time

00:23:33.280 --> 00:23:38.100
Ubawareta kimi no egao

00:23:33.280 --> 00:23:38.100
Your smile has been stolen

00:23:38.100 --> 00:23:41.770
Tori modosu tame ni hashiru yo

00:23:38.100 --> 00:23:41.770
But I will race to get it back

00:23:41.770 --> 00:23:47.710
Boku wa hikari sasu michi wo

00:23:41.770 --> 00:23:47.710
As I run down the shining path

00:24:06.550 --> 00:24:12.000
Next Episode
Covert Ops Under the Night Sky
